 are part of a standard conversation structure applied to all your conversations, such as the welcome greeting or fallback responses. Setup topics run at the appropriate spot in a conversation based on the context, keywords, or utterances entered by the user, and any conditions that are specified for the setup topic.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/conversational-interfaces/virtual-agent/working-setup-topics.html","release":"australia","product":"Virtual Agent","classification":"virtual-agent","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":7,"breadcrumb":["Customizing a chat experience","Configure","Virtual Agent","Conversational Interfaces"],"tags":["#conversational-interfaces","#virtual-agent","#chatbot","#nlu","#topics","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/conversational-interfaces/virtual-agent/working-setup-topics.md"},
